node_modules/
dist/

# Generated report output. `bun run report` writes index.html and corpus.json here,
# together a few MB that regenerate in seconds from the transcripts on the machine.
#
# Ignoring a whole DIRECTORY rather than a list of filenames is deliberate, and it is
# not the same mistake as the bare `*.html` this file used to carry. That pattern
# reached across the entire repo and silently dropped files nobody had decided to
# ignore — the git spelling of `2>/dev/null`. [LAW:no-silent-failure] This rule names
# one path whose entire reason to exist is generated output, so nothing hand-authored
# can wander into its blast radius.
#
# It also means the output can never be committed by accident, which matters here: a
# corpus.json is a verbatim record of one machine's real sessions.
out/

# Machine-local runtime state, never checked in. This lock carries a session UUID, a
# pid and a boot timestamp — facts about one running process on one laptop, with no
# meaning in any other clone. It was tracked until miser-portability-adi.1.
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock

# Addresses the container runtime assigned to a running stack, written by
# telemetry/stack.sh so Prometheus can discover the collector. They describe three
# containers alive on one laptop right now and mean nothing in any other clone —
# the same reason .claude/scheduled_tasks.lock is not tracked.
telemetry/.run/
